menu "Tiercel"

comment "Behaviour"

config TIERCEL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_S
    int "Seconds of inactivity before the idle clock appears"
    range 0 3600
    default 30
    help
      Initial value only; the user changes it under Settings > Clock Timeout
      and it is stored in NVS. 0 never returns to the clock.

config TIERCEL_ALARM_SNOOZE_MIN
    int "Minutes an acknowledged alarm stays quiet"
    range 1 240
    default 10
    help
      Initial value only. A tap on the alert overlay acknowledges every alarm
      on it; one still active after this long is raised again. Changed on the
      device under Settings > Alarm Snooze.

config TIERCEL_DEFAULT_UNITS_CELSIUS
    bool "Default to Celsius"
    default n

config TIERCEL_DEFAULT_THEME_DARK
    bool "Default to the dark theme"
    default y
    help
      The design's default. Changed on the device under Settings > Theme.

comment "Connectivity"

config TIERCEL_MQTT_DEFAULT_PORT
    int "Default MQTT port"
    default 8883
    help
      Headwaters' Mosquitto listens only on 8883, TLS, with a username and
      password. This is what the setup portal starts from.

config TIERCEL_WIFI_TX_POWER_QDBM
    int "Wi-Fi maximum transmit power (quarter-dBm)"
    range 8 80
    default 80
    help
      esp_wifi_set_max_tx_power() takes quarter-dBm: 80 is 20 dBm, the
      driver's default. Lower it only for a unit whose setup AP cannot be
      seen while it can itself see networks -- the signature of a 3V3 rail
      that sags on transmit bursts (Capstan's MaTouch needed 44).

endmenu
